Z||000000||fotofrank||02-26-99||07:59 PM||||Any one know if a late modle GM TBI fits a '84 fiero 4cylender? If so does it improve preformance? 
Z||000001||theogre||03-30-99||06:13 PM||||the 700 family TBI(87-88 Fiero, and others to present) Will Not interchange with the older units. The manifold, Fuel lines, and throtle cable linkages are differant. They are also diferant electrically, as nearly all the connectors have been changed on the 700.<p>I think Holley still hase a TBI that will work, has a larger bore size (higher CFM), and will directly replace all 84-86 Fiero units. The ECM will even work with it correctly w/o modification.
Z||000002||raceknb||04-02-99||10:06 PM||||Check out the Fiero Store on line for the Holley unit.  Just a side note, incase anyone is crazy enough...Mikuni makes a twin 2 bbl downdraft carb set for the v-6.  Supposed to be 30%+ in HP and torque.  Saw one at the SCCA double regionals here in Las Vegas and WOW.  The tope end on this car was intense.  the 60-100 trap speed was right off the charts, but the sacrifice was low end and $$$  The set is supposed to be around $2000.  For a few more peso's...put the 2.8 stoker in and have a blast.  FYI
Z||000003||theogre||04-04-99||03:00 AM||||holley items, including the upgraded TBI, can be researched at  <A HREF="http://www.holley.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.holley.com</A> <p>you can probably find the unit at better prices that fiero store if you shope around. I'like the fact the fiero store, focoa, etc, have some hard to get stuff, but thier prices for common items are hidious.
